text:
mina: Quick design review for the new 'Shroud' dark theme iteration — main goals: micro-token legibility, legend clarity, and copy readability on dense dashboards.

ev an: Can you TL;DR the top 2 failures you saw on staging?

mina: 1) 11px inline tags and model slugs drop out on dim panels. 2) Legends with >6 series are ambiguous; several hues compress into the same perceived tone at small sizes.

keiko: Also saw focus outlines are effectively invisible when modal overlays stack. Keyboard users lose track.

mina: Proposed fixes: 1) scoped micro-backplates for inline tokens (.token-inline) rather than global luminance lifts. 2) dual-encoding chart strategy: color + marker/line-style + compact legend icons. 3) tweak copy in legends to include short parenthetical codes for quick scanning.

roy: Love the parenthetical codes idea (e.g., "latency-p95 (L95)") — helps when color fails. Can you paste a tiny CSS example?

mina: Sure, quick snippet below: 

```css
:root[data-theme=shroud-dark]{
  --panel-bg: #071116;
  --inline-backdrop: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
  --token-small: #e9f3f6;
  --comment-muted: #6f8087;
  --focus-ring: rgba(120,190,255,0.14);
  --chart-base: #2e9bd6, #3fb3a0, #8fc36a, #f2b75a, #c874b0;
  --chart-accents: #ffb86a, #ff6b6b;
}
.inline-token{ background:var(--inline-backdrop); padding:0 6px; border-radius:6px; font-size:11px;}
/* chart: map index -> (color, marker, dash) */
```

keiko: A11y pass? Need token contrast >= 4.5:1 where text is actionable. For purely decorative comments we can allow lower ratios and use italics.

mina: Ran a quick calc: token-small on inline-backdrop over panel-bg ~5.0:1. Comments remain ~3.0:1; will keep them muted + italic.

ev an: For charts, can we ensure marker icons show in compact legends (e.g., small square + code)? That reduces horizontal reliance on color.

roy: Dev note: chart lib supports strokeDasharray + marker mapping. We'll add a theme JSON to map css vars to chart config so toggles don't require full re-render.

keiko: Keyboard focus: propose 2px ring with subtle glow only when using keyboard (prefers-reduced-motion-safe). Keeps it unobtrusive for mouse users.

mina: Testing plan: 12 participants, two tasks: 1) identify the series labeled "errors" on a 7-series chart, 2) copy an 11px inline model slug from a code cell. Measure accuracy + time.

theme-ci: Preview created by @mina: https://staging.redwood-inference.internal/preview/shroud-theme-1967 — includes inline backplates, chart markers/patterns, and keyboard focus tweaks.

ev an: I'll run the microtest tomorrow and share results. If comment contrast flags, fallback to tooltip reveal on hover.

roy: Thanks everyone — please attach before/after screenshots to the PR and include the test script. :thumbsup:
